    ],
    "word_count": 52,
    "html": "<p>Gary Markel is an American insurance businessman and grandson of the founder of Markel Corporation. He held shares in the family insurer and led his own insurance agencies in Florida. Now retired in Naples, he co-founded Operation Healing Forces with his wife Denise to support Special Operations service members and their families.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Gary Markel’s work with military families began after he watched wounded veterans learning to scuba dive on television. He contacted General Doug Brown, who connected him with the Special Operations Command’s Care Coalition. Those conversations led to retreats where injured service members and their partners could spend time together with professional support.\n\nTo make retreats easier to provide, Operation Healing Forces sought donated stays in vacation homes and resorts. Markel and his brother Tony initially covered its administrative and fundraising expenses. The wider board later took on those costs, allowing other donations to fund programmes.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 91,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Direct founder interview and the charity’s subsequent board statement support origin and funding mechanics without claiming clinical efficacy."
    },
    "source_ids": [
