      "S9"
    ],
    "word_count": 95,
    "html": "<p>Gary Markel’s work with military families began after he watched wounded veterans learning to scuba dive on television. He contacted General Doug Brown, who connected him with the Special Operations Command’s Care Coalition. Those conversations led to retreats where injured service members and their partners could spend time together with professional support.</p>\r\n<p>To make retreats easier to provide, Operation Healing Forces sought donated stays in vacation homes and resorts. Markel and his brother Tony initially covered its administrative and fundraising expenses. The wider board later took on those costs, allowing other donations to fund programmes.</p>\r\n"
  },
